message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Block Plugin Engine (BPE)"
type: software
version: "1.0.2"
authors:
  - given-names: Santiago
    family-names: Tapia-Fernández
    affiliation: Universidad Politécnica de Madrid (UPM), CVAR-UPM
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1418-9276"
    email: santiago.tapia@upm.es
abstract: >-
  Block Plugin Engine (BPE) is a C++ execution framework for ROS 2 applications based on dynamically loaded processing blocks. It provides configurable periodic, event-driven and multi-threaded scheduling, concurrent blackboard communication and generic ROS 2 input/output boundaries. Its architecture is designed to support predictable execution and memory behaviour in real-time robotic applications.
license: BSD-3-Clause
